# Linux Shell Input and Output Lab

## Project Overview

This project documents hands-on practice using the Bash shell in an authorized Linux Qwiklabs training environment as part of my cybersecurity studies.

The exercise focused on understanding how commands provide input to the shell and how Linux returns either successful output or error messages.

I practiced generating text output with `echo`, performing integer calculations with `expr`, clearing terminal output with `clear`, and experimenting with Bash syntax beyond the required lab instructions.

During my additional practice, I intentionally attempted a grouped mathematical expression and encountered a Bash syntax error. Investigating the error helped reinforce the distinction between how Bash interprets command syntax and how an individual command processes its arguments.

---

## Skills Demonstrated

- Linux command-line fundamentals
- Bash shell usage
- Command input and output
- Reading terminal output
- Error-message interpretation
- Basic shell syntax
- Integer calculations with `expr`
- String output with `echo`
- Troubleshooting command syntax
- Independent command-line experimentation

